  "sourceFindings": [
    "The default engine remains NativeScript; four old NS test bodies and all42 prior UI method bodies are byte-exact. No creation, array-editor, save, reopen, clear or built-in result-chain helper is changed by this candidate.",
    "Added selectors derive explicit Expo method names and fixture IDs; the same360-second shared case deadline covers both nonempty and empty executions. No new waiting allowance is added.",
    "The new foreground observation reads public XCUIApplication.state after the original nativeListCompletion guard. It records the actual states and requires Shortcuts foreground and MiniApps not foreground without activating either app to manufacture the result.",
    "Expo register serves the real public action table. The handler reads invocation.parameters, rejects non-array/non-scalar/non-finite values, preserves order and records actual caller and invocation.id. It does not receive or synthesize the test expected values or native Int/Double tags.",
    "The actual action channel serializes its supplied UUID in invocation.id; the platform authority binds that action invocation to command.id. Host call context uses the admitted installed package scope; HanlinFileService maps it to HanlinPackages/<installedID>/State.",
    "The fresh validated nonce chooses a single relative State filename; existing bytes cause failure. Unicode JSON is escaped to ASCII without changing the decoded result, the real public state write is awaited and checked, and only then is the identical ordinary JSON result returned.",
    "The source pins preserve the existing authored Expo versions. The existing producer binds actual SDK package versions at build; this review does not infer current hosted ABI or compiler acceptance."
  ],
